            <ArticleTitle>Achieving weight loss and avoiding obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>730-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of the vast variety of nutrients on metabolic outcome and health is complex. A large number of factors play a role in the type and quantity of food consumed in free-living conditions. It is therefore obvious that prescribing a restrictive diet regimen that favours 1 or 2 nutrients at the expense of the others is a poor tool to manage long-term health and weight.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
